WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.291 --> 00:00:03.361
(telephone dialing)

00:00:03.361 --> 00:00:04.656
(telephone ringing)

00:00:04.656 --> 00:00:05.489
- [Male] Hello?

00:00:05.489 --> 00:00:06.979
- [Narrator] Ah, first crushes,

00:00:06.979 --> 00:00:08.376
we all remember them

00:00:08.376 --> 00:00:10.936
and if you're a girl
who grew up in the '90s,

00:00:10.936 --> 00:00:12.776
your first crush might have been

00:00:12.776 --> 00:00:15.170
one of the Dream Phone guys.

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:17.693
- Oh boy, I think Gary.

00:00:17.693 --> 00:00:19.799
He has kind of a nice smile.

00:00:19.799 --> 00:00:22.474
Yeah, I'd say Matt's probably a jock.

00:00:22.474 --> 00:00:23.960
- [Narrator] This is Mike Gray,

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.160
the unlikely inventor

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.677
of the ultimate '90s tween dating game.

00:00:27.677 --> 00:00:31.242
- We knew the game targeted
towards nine-year-old girls.

00:00:31.242 --> 00:00:33.982
It was a bunch of guys that did it

00:00:33.982 --> 00:00:35.659
but that's okay.

00:00:35.659 --> 00:00:38.055
- [Male Voice] I know who
it is but I'm not telling.

00:00:38.055 --> 00:00:41.981
- [Mike] I said, let's do
something that's kind of like Clue

00:00:41.981 --> 00:00:43.403
so it's deduction,

00:00:43.403 --> 00:00:45.085
we're gonna call a bunch of boys

00:00:45.085 --> 00:00:47.918
'cause we heard some boy likes us.

00:00:49.657 --> 00:00:51.608
- [Interviewer] So it all
started with the phone, right?

00:00:51.608 --> 00:00:52.735
- Yes.

00:00:52.735 --> 00:00:54.168
We kind of laughed

00:00:54.168 --> 00:00:56.601
and we kind of called
this the pink slipper.

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:59.426
In its day, it was an
elegant and beautiful thing.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:00.925
- [Male] I know where he hangs out.

00:01:00.925 --> 00:01:02.386
- [Narrator] So how did they pick the boys

00:01:02.386 --> 00:01:04.285
of your teenage dreams?

00:01:04.285 --> 00:01:06.264
- [Mike] We went to a photo house.

00:01:06.264 --> 00:01:08.577
We didn't know, like, who these
boys were or anything.

00:01:08.577 --> 00:01:11.748
We just picked ones that we liked.

00:01:11.748 --> 00:01:13.896
- [Narrator] But that's not
the only '90s girls game

00:01:13.896 --> 00:01:14.916
Mike made.

00:01:14.916 --> 00:01:17.478
He also made the super
successful Mall Madness,

00:01:17.478 --> 00:01:20.877
but he's pretty real about
his influence as a guy.

00:01:20.877 --> 00:01:23.138
- Well, if I'm gonna make
a game about shopping,

00:01:23.138 --> 00:01:24.578
what I know about shopping,

00:01:24.578 --> 00:01:27.560
you just go get what you
need and get back to the car.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.211
Later it was pointed out to me

00:01:29.211 --> 00:01:32.153
that that's kind of not
the way ladies shop.

00:01:32.153 --> 00:01:36.272
So it was kind of in a
funny way a guys game

00:01:36.272 --> 00:01:37.895
but it was for girls.

00:01:37.895 --> 00:01:40.632
I say games are togetherness in a box.

00:01:40.632 --> 00:01:41.810
Play a game with people,

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:43.032
you learn a lot about them

00:01:43.032 --> 00:01:45.453
and it shouldn't be
about winning and losing,

00:01:45.453 --> 00:01:47.128
it should be about being together.

00:01:47.128 --> 00:01:48.312
- [Male] You're right.

00:01:48.312 --> 00:01:50.479
(yelling)

